If you're going to do the protection racket, gnomes are the best choice
for wizards.

But the protection racket is a bad percentage play (though it _is_
worth playing for a while to learn the tactics involved), and none of
the top players do it normally unless they're doing a pure pacifist
ascension.

For me, the strength bonus for humans overwhelms all the other racial
bonuses, but infravision is quite nice so if you're struggling in the
early game then going non-human is a reasonable choice.



